## 6. *Summary of Inferences*

## 7. *Binom test- Inference test for a single proportion*

Null hypothesis: 50% of the students believe in God.
Alternative hypothesis: The proportion of students who believe in God is either less than or more than 50%.



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
mosaic::binom.test(~ believe_in_god, data = god_modified, success = "Yes")
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```



data:  god_modified$believe_in_god  [with success = Yes]
number of successes = 26, number of trials = 41, p-value = 0.1173
alternative hypothesis: true probability of success is not equal to 0.5
95 percent confidence interval:
 0.4693625 0.7787721
sample estimates:
probability of success 
             0.6341463 
```


:::
:::

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
